      "title": "Kulgam encounter: LeT commander Lateef Bhat trapped, refuses to surrender",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/fresh-encounter-in-j-k-s-kulgam-as-security-forces-track-escaped-terrorist-126111800089_1.html",
      "description": "An encounter broke out between security forces and terrorists on Wednesday in Jammu and Kashmir's Kulgam district, where a terrorist was killed in a gunfight two days ago, police said.\n\"#Encounter started with terrorists and joint party of JKP and SF in Kulgam,\" Kashmir Zone Police said in a post on X.\nOn Monday, security forces killed Umar Nisar Dar, one of the terrorists involved in the November 11 attack on CRPF personnel in Kulgam.\nAnother terrorist, Lateef Bhat, one of the most wanted and the only surviving local terrorist in Kashmir valley, managed to escape the cordon at the Laru bypass area.\nWhile there was no exchange of gunfire since Monday, security forces continued a massive search operation in a vast area around the encounter site to track and neutralise Bhat.\nDuring the searches on early Wednesday morning, contact with the terrorists was established, leading to a renewed firefight that is ongoing.\nAccording to officials, Dar allegedly provided shelter and logistical",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-18T02:47:50"
